# Print-in-place fit proof: the plunger must be a free captive body clearing
# the fixed frame (race walls, bridged rail, arch tip) and both jaws (pin
# arms, pin posts) at rest. `fitcheck` renders plunger ∩ (frame + jaws) and
# must be EMPTY. `fitcheck_neg` grows the race walls onto the blade so it MUST
# overlap, proving the check can fail.
#
# `drive_mouth` proves the CAM is connected: the pin's own swept body above
# the blade's −y edge must be free of plunger material — the notch has to
# open through that edge or the pin is never driven. A tangent/short notch
# cuts nothing there while every other gate stays green (found on this very
# design: watertight, sliced clean, jaws that could not close).
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
drive_mouth   empty
